                  "id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50NzQ3ODk3",
                  "databaseId": 747897,
                  "body": "Hi. I suggest 3 approaches to try:\r\n\r\n## 1. Config\r\n\r\nWe can try to add `import 'newrelic'` to the top of `nuxt.config.js`? This should partially work as this is almost the topmost entry-point. \r\n\r\n## 2. CLI Wrapper\r\n\r\nWe may create a custom cli wrapper in the root of the project:\r\n\r\n`~/nuxt.js`:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nrequire('newrelic')\r\nrequire('nuxt/bin/nuxt')\r\n````\r\n\r\nAnd then inside `package.json`:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\nscripts: {\r\n-- \"start\": \"nuxt start\",\r\n++ \"start\": \"node ./nuxt start\",\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 3. Module (best)\r\n\r\nIf newrelic is similar to sentry, this is not **required** to be the first import, we can do this via a nuxt module and it globally should register itself to the entire process:\r\n\r\n`modules/newrelic.js`\r\n\r\n```js\r\nexport default async function() {\r\n  await import('newrelic')\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n`nuxt.config.js`\r\n\r\n```js\r\nexport default {\r\n    modules: [\r\n        '~/modules/newrelic'\r\n    ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n",
                  "createdAt": "2019-08-15T17:39:22Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/nuxt/nuxt/discussions/9303#discussioncomment-747897",
