                {
                  "id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50NzQ3OTE0",
                  "databaseId": 747914,
                  "body": "I would take a look at how we handle in the Sentry module as inspiration: https://github.com/nuxt-community/sentry-module/blob/master/lib/module.js#L60-L73\r\n\r\nTo test easily without having to write a module, you can directly use hooks directly in your `nuxt.config.js`, example:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nexport default {\r\n  hooks: {\r\n    'render:errorMiddleware'(app) {\r\n      app.use((err, req, res, next) => {\r\n        // Catch the error with you error reported\r\n        console.error(`An error occured while rendering ${req.url}\\n`, err)\r\n        // Let Nuxt show the error page\r\n        // You can customize the HTML error page for production by creating app/views/error.html\r\n        next(err)\r\n      })\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```",
                  "createdAt": "2020-11-10T11:28:13Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/nuxt/nuxt/discussions/9303#discussioncomment-747914",
