                {
                  "id": "MDE3OkRpc2N1c3Npb25Db21tZW50NzQ3OTE4",
                  "databaseId": 747918,
                  "body": "I didn't create a plugin because on further inspection it might not be neccesary to set the names on each request, though in my system I have the configuration that was quoted above.\r\n\r\nSince the change in configuration from some versions ago, you can just try to import newrelic in top of nuxt.config.js.\r\n\r\nAnd if you need further customization, use a hook like\r\n\r\n```\r\nhooks: {\r\n    'render:route' (url, result, context) {\r\n      try {\r\n        newrelic.setTransactionName(url)\r\n      } catch (error) {\r\n        // Ignore\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n\r\nPlease let me know what worked for you, so we can create a final and updated answer to anyone trying to setup newrelic with nuxt, and make a plugin if deemed neccesary :)",
                  "createdAt": "2021-05-17T12:45:43Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/nuxt/nuxt/discussions/9303#discussioncomment-747918",
